{
  "contract": "upcoming-tiers",
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "The shared definition of what 'upcoming' means, for Mac, iOS, and web.",
    "One feed (GET /api/calendar/upcoming) answers two different questions --",
    "'what should I do now' and 'what is on my plate' -- and the bug this table",
    "exists to prevent is answering the first with the head of the second. Every",
    "client implements `classifyUpcoming` and must reproduce these rows exactly.",
    "Swift: Sources/MeetingFocus.swift. TypeScript: packages/contracts/src/upcoming.ts.",
    "Product knobs: packages/contracts/src/upcoming-config.json."
  ],
  "rules": [
    "AGENDA: a timed event is on the agenda when it has an end still ahead of",
    "`now`, a real title (not '', 'block', 'blank' or '(no title)'), and a",
    "readable start on today or tomorrow. All-day and Hidden-from-Next events",
    "are excluded from Upcoming.",
    "Sorted by start, falling back to end, with",
    "undated and farther-ahead events omitted and ties broken by id.",
    "TIER: purely temporal, and anchored to civil days in `timeZone` -- never to a",
    "duration. now = started and not ended. today = starts later on today's date.",
    "tomorrow = starts on tomorrow's date. Farther-ahead and unscheduled events",
    "stay in Calendar rather than appearing on this two-day surface.",
    "FOCUS: the hero slot -- the countdown, the call to action. It is the first",
    "agenda event that is tier `now` or `today`. Nothing else",
    "may ever occupy it. A null focus is a closed day:",
    "the surface collapses the hero to a summary and renders the rest as a list.",
    "Note what focus does NOT require: a join link. An in-person meeting is still",
    "what is next; it simply has no button.",
    "MEMBER: Home shows only events the member organizes or attends and has not",
    "declined, applied to each copy before copies collapse. An event on the",
    "member's own calendar (`primary`, or `acct:<account>:primary`) stays unless",
    "the guest row marked `self` says `declined`; an event there with no guests",
    "(an own block, a flight) stays. An event on a subscribed feed (`sub:`) stays:",
    "the member switched the feed on for Upcoming. An event on any other calendar",
    "(a colleague's, a shared or imported Google calendar) is dropped: there",
    "Google's `self` marks that calendar's owner, and an event the member is on",
    "also sits on their own calendar. A row with no `attendees` field carries no",
    "participation facts and is not judged. Swift `MeetingFocus.isMemberEvent`,",
    "TypeScript `isMemberEvent`, Kotlin `Upcoming.isMemberEvent`.",
    "JOIN WINDOW: the hero's button exists only from `joinWindowMinutes` before",
    "the start (upcoming-config.json) until the end. Outside it the hero is a",
    "countdown, and the room card's Start holds the accent instead -- one accent",
    "per screen. Inside it the button carries the countdown and joins in the app:",
    "your own room as host, a colleague's Meet room as a knock, anything else",
    "through its own app. Swift `MeetingFocus.canJoin`, TypeScript `canJoin`."
  ],
  "eventFields": {
    "id": "stable identity, and the tie-break for equal starts",
    "title": "checked against the placeholder list",
    "start": "ISO 8601, or null for an event with no readable start",
    "end": "ISO 8601; an event with no readable end is never on the agenda",
    "allDay": "all-day events are always excluded from upcoming",
    "demoted": "owner-wide 'Hide from Next'; excluded from Upcoming, remains in Calendar",
    "joinable": "has a video link; affects the call to action, never the tiering",
    "calendarId": "optional; the feed's calendar id: `primary`, `acct:<account>:primary`, `sub:<feed>`, or another Google calendar id",
    "attendees": "optional; the guest list as `{ status, self }` rows, `[]` for no guests. Absent: the row is not judged by the member rule"
  },
  "expectFields": {
    "canJoin": "optional; by event id, whether `canJoin(event, now)` is true. Only the events listed are checked."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an in-progress meeting holds the hero",
